    <statement><p>Find the first partial derivatives of the function <m>\displaystyle f(x,y) = \frac{3 x}{(x+y)^{2}}.</m></p>
<p><alert> 1.</alert> <m>\displaystyle f_x(x,y) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert> 2.</alert> <m>\displaystyle f_y(x,y) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{3\mathopen{}\left(x+y\right)^{2}-3\cdot 2x\mathopen{}\left(x+y\right)^{1}}{\left(x+y\right)^{2\cdot 2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-3\cdot 2x}{\left(x+y\right)^{3}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
